# Build an Assassin and photograph his weapon proficiencies, which is half of
# bd inc-tek.8.3 finding PA-03-F11: seven prestige classes promise
# proficiencies in their prose and only one of them declares the field.
#
# The Assassin's prose promises "crossbows and light weapons"
# (lib/prestige.irh:509). Before the fix the class had no Proficiencies: line
# at all, so it granted neither. The fix declares
#   Proficiencies: WG_CROSSBOWS, WG_LIGHT;      lib/prestige.irh:583
# and WG_CROSSBOWS is a group that had to be invented, because the three
# crossbows sat in WG_SIMPLE|WG_ARCHERY and WG_EXOTIC and no group named them.
#
# THE ORACLE is the sheet's Proficiencies line, which src/Sheet.cpp:861-876
# builds by walking the character's proficiency bits against
# WeaponGroupNames[] (src/Tables.cpp:1329). "Crossbows" is the row added for
# the new bit.
#
# KNOWN AND EXPECTED: only Crossbows will print, not "light weapons".
# WG_LIGHT has no row in WeaponGroupNames at all, so it never prints for
# anybody -- that is bd inc-tek.15, a separate defect found while fixing this
# one. The grant is real either way; it just cannot be read off this line.
#
# SEED. The attribute rolls and the offered feats vary with the seed, so the
# feat picks stay positional and a seed is passed.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Rogue"
a                       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
@choose "Neutral"       # the class refuses a Good alignment
@choose "Alertness"
@until "Unspent Skill Ranks" a          # however many feats are asked for

# Eighteen ranks, two to a skill. The four the Assassin's gate reads first;
# the rest only because character generation will not release a character
# with a rank unspent.
@cursorto:mark "Disguise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Poison Use" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Bluff" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Alchemy" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Appraise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Balance" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Climb" DOWN
RIGHT*3
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d                               # character sheet
@until "Class  Rogue 5" G       # five core levels, for the ranks they carry

# The gate wants Disguise 10, Poison Use 10, Hide 7 and Move Silently 7.
# ISkillLevel (src/Create.cpp:3955) counts training and the inherent
# attribute bonus as well as ranks, so filling each to its cap clears them.
S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Disguise" DOWN
RIGHT*8
@cursorto:mark "Poison Use" DOWN
RIGHT*8
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" UP
RIGHT*8
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" UP
RIGHT*8
ENTER y

P                               # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Assassin"
@expect "Assassin 0"            # the gate let him in

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Assassin"
@while "Choose a feat" a

# The Assassin's 1st level hands over a spellbook (lib/prestige.irh:597-607).
# The item lands in the In-the-Air slot, and the game will not leave
# inventory mode while anything is there -- so it must be stowed before any
# further keystroke is spent, or every key after it goes into the inventory
# screen instead. Leave the sheet to let the prompt surface, stow, leave
# inventory, and come back.
ESC
@while "Air':?" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@until "Skill Ratings" d

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Assassin"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@expect "Assassin 2"

W                       # Write Dump
a s s n ENTER           # filename: "assn"
ESC
@quit
